<h1>React Router → Filesystem Routing</h1>
<p style="color:var(--ui-text-muted);margin-bottom:1rem">The file's path is the URL. Zero configuration.</p>

<div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:2rem">
  <div>
    <h3>React/Next.js</h3>
    <pre style="background:#1e1e2e;color:#cdd6f4;padding:1rem;border-radius:8px;font-size:0.8rem;overflow-x:auto;line-height:1.6"><code>// Next.js App Router requires:
app/
  page.tsx          // Home
  layout.tsx        // Root layout
  loading.tsx       // Loading state
  error.tsx         // Error boundary
  not-found.tsx     // 404
  blog/
    page.tsx        // Blog list
    [slug]/
      page.tsx      // Blog detail
      loading.tsx   // Loading for this route
      error.tsx     // Error for this route

// 5 special file conventions
// Nested layouts, parallel routes,
// intercepting routes, route groups...</code></pre>
  </div>
  <div>
    <h3>PRESTO</h3>
    <pre style="background:#1e1e2e;color:#cdd6f4;padding:1rem;border-radius:8px;font-size:0.8rem;overflow-x:auto;line-height:1.6"><code>pages/
  index.htx         // Home (/)
  _layout.htx       // Layout
  _404.htx          // Not found
  blog/
    index.htx       // Blog list (/blog)
    [slug].htx      // Blog detail (/blog/:slug)

// One file per route.
// One file handles ALL concerns:
//   data, rendering, layout, errors.
// No loading.tsx (page arrives complete).
// No error.tsx (errors at the server level).
// No special conventions beyond _layout.</code></pre>
  </div>
</div>

<h3 style="margin-top:2rem">This page's route</h3>
<p style="font-family:monospace;background:#f5f5f5;padding:0.75rem;border-radius:6px">
  File: <code>pages/reorientation/routing.htx</code><br>
  URL: <code>/reorientation/routing</code><br>
  Configuration: <strong>none</strong>
</p>

<p style="margin-top:1.5rem"><a href="/reorientation">&larr; All reorientations</a></p>
